r10itype — interface-typed port OF AN INTERFACE (§ ifaceIfaceTypedPort)

Purpose-built goldens behind the InterfType conversion.  Build each with

  surelog -parse -mt 0 -mp 0 -d uhdm <f>.sv -o out      # folded (default mode)
  surelog -parse -mt 0 -mp 0 -d uhdm -elabuhdm <f>.sv   # testflags mode

and compare `uhdm-dump` against `slang-uhdm <f>.sv --single-unit -o o.uhdm`.

t1  three ports on one interface container (two interface-typed + one logic),
    positional connection.  Pins: nested view = enclosing MODULE line col 0
    (module top line 18 -> work@top.u_c.aa 18:0, though u_c is instantiated
    at line 23); parameters listed ONCE on the nested view; LowConn anchors
    at the PORT DECL for a MULTI-port positional connection.
    OPEN residues (both pre-date this feature): golden emits NO ref_module for
    u_c in work@top's def view while we emit one with three ports, and the
    regular `clk` port's elab LowConn anchors at the port decl, not the conn.

t2  both write-order directions in ONE file — acont(<zsub) and zcont(>asub).
    Pins § ifaceIfaceTypedPortOrder: an INTERFACE container's def-view port
    LowConn binds the sub-interface's DEF interface_inst only when the sub
    def name sorts BEFORE the container's; otherwise it binds the port's own
    bare net.  InterfType is the net half (tnoc_flit_if < tnoc_types).
    Also pins that the folded (no -elabuhdm) HighConn actual is the col-0
    tail dup while -elabuhdm binds the home view.

t5  MODULE container, aif < mmid.   t6  MODULE container, amid < zzif.
    Together they show the order rule does NOT apply to modules: every
    interface is written before every module, so a module port always binds
    the interface_inst.  Both already matched before this change.

t7  MODPORT-qualified interface-typed port of an interface (abus.man).
    The DEF view now matches (net minted, no vpiTypedef, LowConn -> modport).
    The ELAB view is still UNMODELLED — golden adds a port whose HighConn is
    a hier_path (u_b.man) with two ref_obj actuals, a LowConn ref_obj named
    <enclosing module>.<port> bound to the modport, an interface_typespec
    (modport, vpiIsModPort) typedef over a base interface_typespec, AND a
    shadow interface_inst work@top.<port> at the enclosing module line col 0
    (cloned vars + the connected modport, parented at the MODULE, weakly
    referenced only).  216 raw dump lines.
